# MatchOnce on a rule that changes a state, not a deletion (bngsim issue #1525).
#
# Two homodimer pools of X0, each flipping one subunit's s from 0 to 1 at k.
# Jmo carries {MatchOnce}: BNG2.pl's network gives it one reaction per complex
# at k. Wpl does not: BNG2.pl gives it 2*k, one reaction per subunit. NFsim's
# per-complex count for MatchOnce never took effect, so Jmo ran at 2*k too.
#
# Uctx makes Z at k per U homodimer, with the dimer as pure context: NFsim counts
# a context reactant once per complex already when it tracks complexes, so the
# MatchOnce on it must not thin it a second time. Z(t) = k*X0*t, 1000 at t = 500.
#
# JLmo is Jmo with a local-function rate read on the whole species, k for every
# complex: NFsim ignored MatchOnce on a local-function rule, so it ran at 2*k.
begin model
begin parameters
  k   1e-3
  X0  2000
end parameters
begin molecule types
  J(d,s~0~1)
  W(d,s~0~1)
  U(d)
  Y()
  Z()
  JL(d,s~0~1)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  J(d!1,s~0).J(d!1,s~0)  X0
  W(d!1,s~0).W(d!1,s~0)  X0
  U(d!1).U(d!1)          X0
  Y()                    1
  JL(d!1,s~0).JL(d!1,s~0)  X0
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules J1 J(s~1)
  Molecules W1 W(s~1)
  Molecules Zt Z()
  Molecules JL1 JL(s~1)
end observables
begin functions
  fjl(x) = if(JL1(x) >= 0, k, 0)
end functions
begin reaction rules
  Jmo: {MatchOnce}J(d!1,s~0).J(d!1,s~0) -> J(d!1,s~1).J(d!1,s~0) k
  Wpl: W(d!1,s~0).W(d!1,s~0) -> W(d!1,s~1).W(d!1,s~0) k
  Uctx: {MatchOnce}U(d!1).U(d!1) + Y() -> U(d!1).U(d!1) + Y() + Z() k
  JLmo: %x:{MatchOnce}JL(d!1,s~0).JL(d!1,s~0) -> JL(d!1,s~1).JL(d!1,s~0) fjl(x)
end reaction rules
end model
generate_network({overwrite=>1})
writeXML()
